The Mercedes-Benz Vito 122 CDi is primarily associated with the W639 generation (2003-2014), specifically the facelifted models from 2010 onwards. It is powered by a 3.0-litre V6 turbo-diesel engine (OM642) producing 165 kW (224 hp) and 440 Nm (325 lb-ft) of torque. It is typically paired with a 5-speed automatic transmission and rear-wheel drive. Some sources mention a 0-62 mph time of 9.1 seconds. Top speed is around 124 mph (200 km/h). Fuel consumption is reported around 32.5-34.2 mpg combined (8.3-8.6 L/100km). CO2 emissions are around 221-232 g/km.

The W639 Vito comes in various lengths (4748mm to 5223mm) and wheelbases (3200mm or 3430mm). It is available in panel van, crew cab (Dualiner), and passenger (Kombi/Traveliner) body styles. Cargo space is substantial, ranging from 4.65 to 6.6 cubic metres depending on configuration. Seating can be up to 9 in passenger versions. Ground clearance is around 146mm (5.7 inches). Turning circle is around 11.8 to 12.5 meters (38.7 to 41 feet).

Safety features on the W639 Vito included standard ABS and ESP. Driver airbags were standard, with passenger and side/curtain airbags often optional. When optioned with side head-protecting airbags, the W639 Vito/Viano could achieve a 5-star ANCAP safety rating. ADAS features were limited compared to modern vehicles, though some later models or optional extras included things like PARKTRONIC (parking sensors).

Interior features were functional, typical of a commercial vehicle, though passenger versions offered more comfort. Features like air conditioning, power windows, cruise control, and a multi-function steering wheel were available. Infotainment was basic by today's standards, typically featuring a standard radio or an optional COMAND system with navigation and Bluetooth. Aftermarket upgrades are available.

Reliability of the OM642 V6 engine is generally considered decent, but some common issues like oil cooler leaks and swirl flap problems have been reported. The 5-speed automatic transmission (722.6) is generally robust but requires regular fluid changes.

